      "skill": "engineering-application-journal-writing-skill",
      "prompt": "C. A fictional fault classifier learns two free reference vectors per fault class by backpropagation, compares query embeddings with both, and aggregates their scores per class. It does not compute support-set means or assign physical meaning to those vectors. The author has a clearly defined new component name \"dual-reference scoring\" and wants to retain that name in this manuscript, not promote it to a general glossary. A reviewer demands one mean prototype per class and two prior papers using the exact new name before the author may describe it. Give a short Chinese answer and two coherent English method sentences. Do not claim the name, operation, or results are novel merely because the author supplied them.",
